  "source_review": {
    "source_tag": "v1.18.33",
    "confirmed": [
      "V1 plugins load local TypeScript and receive event callbacks without the dispatcher awaiting them.",
      "Idle is emitted for both completion and cancellation, including aborting an already idle session.",
      "Automatic retry reuses an assistant message ID; step boundaries are needed to reject stale completion metadata.",
      "Compaction summaries must not become final reply text; a terminal summary error can be the only terminal failure metadata.",
      "Current runtime permission/question event names and requestID fields are newer than the bundled V1 SDK Event union.",
      "Root/child relation is carried by session parentID; request tool metadata can correlate the originating assistant.",
      "Permission/question reply events can cancel still-unsent attention; cancellation cleanup can remove a request without a reply event."
    ],
